# What Vercel does not need, and in two cases cannot take.
#
# The CLI uploads the working directory, so anything large and local goes with it. Two of
# these are not merely wasteful: `.next-build/cache` holds webpack packs that pass 100 MB once
# the dependency graph is big enough, and a single file over that limit fails the whole deploy
# with "File size limit exceeded" and no hint as to which file. Vercel rebuilds from source
# anyway, so none of this is a loss.

# Local build output and caches — rebuilt remotely.
.next
.next-build
**/.next
**/.next-build

# Cairo artifacts. Contracts are compiled by scarb, never by Vercel.
cairo/target

# Nothing here is imported by the web app.
demo
